177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The population of Sierra Leone is 7,541,641 according to the Medium Term Population and Housing Census 2022 \(StatSL, 2022\). The project area comprises two districts, Karene District in the northwest with a population of 290,312 \(4% of the total population\), and Moyamba in the southern region with 346,771 inhabitants \(5% of the total population\). )
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Moyamba district has the largest poultry population in the southern region and is the district with the second highest poultry population in the country   Vegetables are also grown extensively in the district. Karene is the youngest district in the country and is very poor but is known for its small livestock farming. Food insecurity has worsened over the last decade for most people in Sierra Leone and in does district in particular In both Karene and Moyamba, farmers complain of declining yields and loss of soil fertility in a changing environment. The community's over-dependence on conventional agriculture \(due to lack of access to agricultural inputs such as fertilisers, improved crops, finance, knowledge, and farming skills\) leads to low yields and consequently high food insecurity in the face of climate change. In Sierra Leone, only 4% of farmers use irrigation to increase the production of their agricultural produce, with only 1% in Karene and 0.3% in Moyamba using some form of irrigation . )
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In Karene District in particular, poultry farming is already a widespread activity, especially for poor women, as poultry farming requires little input. The main problems in poultry farming are New Cattle Disease \(NCD\) as well as dwarfism of the animals, poor housing, free range \(due to high losses of animals from birds of prey and snakes, among others\), and general lack of care, especially in terms of feeding. As a result, it is estimated that more than 50% of chickens are lost \(EU-BAFS, 2018\). )
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In line to this backdrop, MADAM and SLAWS have received funding from WHH/BMZ to implement a 3 years project to Promote Sustainable Food and Nutrition Security through Climate Smart Livestock farming in Moyamba and Karene District in other to address the overarching situation of our local farmers)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
