/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (During this Quarter reporting period, 2,000 women received training on VSLA methodology and equipment kit support in Moyamba and Kareneh districts. MADAM/SLAWS As implementing partners through the support they have received from WHH/BMZ commenced the rollout of VSLA methodology community-level training with full VSLA equipment kits in 40 project communities, 20 communities in Kareneh and 20 communities in Moyamba district respectively. As the training happened in the two districts including Moyamba and Kareneh, Every community is hosting a total of two VSLA groups making it altogether 80 newly formed VSLA groups which the PSuFONS project has already established in the two districts and support them with training facilities and equipment to run the groups. A three-day training session was set aside for every community with 25 female members per VSLA group. Now all the 80 VSLA groups are functional and operatives.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
