314 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Radio and TV Programmes on climate-friendly agriculture)
/E (Radio and TV Programmes on climate-friendly agriculture)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (During this Quarterly reporting period, the conduct of the first quarterly LIVE TELEVISION BROADCAST PROGRAM at Africa Young Voices AYV and broadcast of radio at 98.1 FM including district media house was fully conducted. On the popularization of the project, activities were conducted at the national level. As the VISIBILITY of every project implementation is one key approach for project sustainability, part of our project activities is to regularly host live TELEVISION and RADIO programs with a national audience of viewers and listeners both direct and indirect participants to create awareness raising on technical issues around the project implementations. At AYV, and during this reporting period, we have commenced the kick-start of our planned quarterly television and radio programs, attracting direct and indirect project participants nationwide. The project manager Mr. Momoh Lawrence Turay MADAM,including the Director of SLAWS Dr. Gudish Jalloh including personnel from the ministry of Agriculture and ministry of fisheries were part of the panelist for both television and radio live discussion. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The television and radio programs on climate-adapted agriculture will widely help to increase awareness and knowledge focused on project intervention and consolidate the learning content plus providing an enabling environment for complaints redress mechanism. Key topics discussed are the project objectives and overview, conservation agriculture, crop intensification, water Management and harvesting, post-harvest management, on-farm feed production, integrated fish and poultry farming, and vegetable production including livestock breeding and management)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
